          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "11.1.1 Phases of the Moon"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.514,
            0.512,
            0.885,
            0.808
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You may have observed that the bright portion of the Moon decreases from a full circle to a half circle in about a week, as shown in Fig. 11.2. The bright portion continues to shrink for another week until it is no longer visible. This two-week period is called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "waning",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " period of the Moon. Different names are given to the Moon’s visible shapes during this cycle (Fig. 11.2). The day when the Moon appears as a full bright circle is called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "full Moon",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " day (or Purnima), and the day when it is not visible is called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "new Moon",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " day (or Amavasya)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.514,
            0.808,
            0.885,
            0.902
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "After the new Moon, its bright side grows to a half circle in about a week and to a full circle (full Moon) in another week. The period when the bright part of the Moon increases is called the"
            }
          ]
        },
